# BCIR C++ style — LLVM base (this is an MLIR/LLVM out-of-tree project), widened to a
# 100-column limit to match the prevailing line width in mlir/lib and runtime/cpp.
#
# Scope (a measured policy, 2026-09-04 dependency audit F9):
#   * applies to the C++ rails — mlir/lib, mlir/include, mlir/tools and runtime/cpp — where
#     LLVM style is the intent of the code (2-space indent, `Type *x`, braces on the statement
#     line). Those trees were reformatted once under this file so the pre-commit hook restyles
#     nothing it does not have to; ReflowComments is off so hand-wrapped comment blocks stay,
#     and BreakStringLiterals is off so a formatter pass never changes the token stream (a
#     literal split in two is two tokens, not whitespace).
#   * does NOT apply to the freestanding C runtime, runtime/c/: that rail is written in a
#     deliberately dense hand-formatted C (several statements per line, no space after `if`,
#     `,` or around operators) that no clang-format configuration describes — every LLVM-based
#     configuration measured rewrote 58k+ lines of its 31k — so the hook does not match it.
#     Reformatting runtime/c is a dedicated decision with its own PR, not a side effect of a hook.
# Run via pre-commit (clang-format hook, pinned to the LLVM 23 line) or: clang-format -i <file>.
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
ColumnLimit: 100
IndentWidth: 2
TabWidth: 2
UseTab: Never
PointerAlignment: Right
DerivePointerAlignment: false
Cpp11BracedListStyle: true
BreakTemplateDeclarations: Yes
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: Inline
ReflowComments: false
BreakStringLiterals: false
SortIncludes: CaseSensitive
SpaceBeforeParens: ControlStatements
---
Language: Cpp
Standard: Latest
